From 26d6d791bc149490d2e77c7c3026fd69d162ec4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ibrahimMohamed124 <ibrahimrs1234@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:31:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(orders): restore stock when an order is cancelled
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Previously OrdersRepository.updateStatus() only flipped the order's
status column — CheckoutRepository already decrements stockQuantity
inside a transaction when an order is placed, but nothing reversed
that decrement when the order was later cancelled (by an admin via
PATCH /orders/:id/status or by the customer via PATCH /orders/:id/cancel).
Net effect: a cancelled order permanently kept its stock deducted.

- OrdersRepository.updateStatus() now accepts an optional
  restockItems list; when present, the status update and the stock
  increment for each item run inside the same $transaction, so a
  failure on either side rolls back both. Uses product.updateMany()
  (not update()) so a since-deleted product is skipped instead of
  throwing P2025 and aborting the whole transaction.
- OrdersService computes restockItems from the order's snapshot items
  only when the transition is an actual PROCESSING/SHIPPED -> CANCELLED
  move (current.status !== status), not on an idempotent re-cancel of
  an already-CANCELLED order — otherwise stock would be restored twice.
  Applied to both the admin updateStatus() path and the customer-facing
  cancelForUser() path.
- orders.service.spec.ts: added coverage for admin cancel + restock,
  customer self-cancel + restock, and the double-restock idempotency
  guard on repeated cancellation.
