From b0c05ebd2efb05d73fd36946149c3d9aa5c17436 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ibrahimMohamed124 <ibrahimrs1234@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 10:32:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(reviews): compute verified from delivered orders
 instead of hardcoded false
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ReviewsService.create() previously left verified: false unconditionally
with a TODO saying Orders module didn't exist yet to check against — it
does now, and the TODO was stale.

- OrdersRepository.hasDeliveredOrderForProduct(userId, productId):
  looks for an OrderItem with the given productId on an order (a)
  owned by the same user and (b) in DELIVERED status. Deliberately
  requires DELIVERED, not just 'has an order containing this product'
  — otherwise anyone could get a verified review by adding the item
  to an order and cancelling it immediately.
- ReviewsModule now imports OrdersModule (already exported
  OrdersRepository, no changes needed there) to inject it into
  ReviewsService. No circular dependency: OrdersModule has no import
  back to ReviewsModule or ProductsModule.
- ReviewsService.create() calls hasDeliveredOrderForProduct() and uses
  the result as the review's verified flag instead of the literal
  false.
- reviews.service.spec.ts (new): covers verified=true with a delivered
  order, verified=false with none, the existing duplicate-review
  rejection, and the product-not-found 404 short-circuiting before the
  orders lookup.
